        "id": "p32-q5-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the area between the curve $y=e^x+e^{-x}$ and the $x$-axis, from $x=-2$ to $x=2$. Give your answer exactly and to 2 decimal places.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2(e^2-e^{-2})\\text{ units}^2\\approx14.51\\text{ units}^2$",
          "worked": "$e^x+e^{-x}>0$ for all $x$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}A&=\\int_{-2}^{2}(e^x+e^{-x})\\,dx\\\\&=[e^x-e^{-x}]_{-2}^{2}\\\\&=(e^2-e^{-2})-(e^{-2}-e^2)\\\\&=2(e^2-e^{-2})\\text{ units}^2\\\\&\\approx14.51\\text{ units}^2.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p32-q5-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the area between the curve $y=x^2+e^x$ and the $x$-axis, from $x=-3$ to $x=3$. Give your answer exactly and to 2 decimal places.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(18+e^3-e^{-3})\\text{ units}^2\\approx38.04\\text{ units}^2$",
          "worked": "$x^2+e^x>0$ for all $x$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}A&=\\int_{-3}^{3}(x^2+e^x)\\,dx\\\\&=\\left[\\frac{x^3}{3}+e^x\\right]_{-3}^{3}\\\\&=(9+e^3)-(-9+e^{-3})\\\\&=18+e^3-e^{-3}\\text{ units}^2\\\\&\\approx38.04\\text{ units}^2.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 31
      }
    ]
  },
